"mermaid-diagram theming" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Mermaid diagram
		<header>A Mermaid diagram draws a flowchart, a sequence, a timeline or any other kind of diagram Mermaid knows, from the element's own text or a file on this site.</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			The `spell` theme's colours ARE Spell UI's tokens, read from the page as it draws:  the primary colour and its
			background for boxes, the text colour for words, the surfaces for groups, yellow for notes.  So a theme picked
			in the menu above, or edited in the theme editor, reaches the diagram too;  switching the page to dark draws
			it again, dark.

			Its own tokens are the box's:  `--ui-mermaid-diagram-padding`, and how faint the last good drawing is under
			an error, `--ui-mermaid-diagram-stale-opacity`.
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-mermaid-diagram" playground></>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Mermaid's own themes are offered beside Spell's (`theme`), by their own names.  A light one with a dark twin
			follows the page:  `default` draws as `dark` on a dark page, `neo` as `neo-dark`, `redux` as
			`redux-dark`, `redux-color` as `redux-dark-color`.  `neutral` and `forest` draw the same either way.

			The pictures in Spell's READMEs are drawn in the same Spell look, from the same table of colours
			(`yarn mermaid:pretty`), so a README and a page match.
		</>
	</>
